                                [...]

While I have argued against confirmation, I now find that this solution
to the problem really makes sense to me.  I think, however, that it might
be good to simply modify the movement commends rather than toggling back
and forth between fight and move modes.

Here is my suggestion:

Change the upper-case movement command from "move forever and attack anything
in your way" into a new movement mode - "move aggressively into the neighbor-
ing square, attacking anything in your way, jumping into any water that is
there, etc."  The current upper-case movement definition is crazy anyway,
anyone in their right mind should use <ctl>-movement, not <shft>-movement
as currently implemented.

So as long as you are using the lower-case movement commands you will
never attack or jump into water (unless blind or confused or hallucinating).
<shft>-move is an aggressive move and *will* move you into water and will
attack any neighboring creature.  <ctl>-move would act the same as it
currently does.  <ctl>-<shft>-move would combine the extended movement
mode of <ctl> with the aggressive mode of <shft>, reproducing the same
mode of movement as the current <shft>-move (for anyone crazy enough to
want to move this way)  ;^).

Any comments?  I personally feel that this proposed movement system is
consistent and makes a lot of sense, and would actually improve gameplay.

